course: world
lesson: 4
title: The solar system and the planets
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The solar system is the Sun and everything that goes around it: eight planets, their moons, dwarf planets such as Pluto, asteroids and comets.
explain: In order from the Sun the planets are Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune: a way to remember them is «My Very Easy Method Just Speeds Up Naming».
explain: The four inner planets are small and made of rock; the four outer planets are giants made mostly of gas or ice, with no solid ground to stand on.
explain: The farther a planet is from the Sun, the longer its year: Mercury goes around in 88 days, but Neptune needs about 165 of our years.
explain: If the Sun were a football, the Earth would be a peppercorn about 25 metres away, and Neptune would be about three quarters of a kilometre away.
fact: The solar system is the Sun and everything that moves around it.
fact: There are eight planets in the solar system.
fact: Mercury is the planet closest to the Sun.
fact: Neptune is the planet farthest from the Sun.
fact: Jupiter is the biggest planet.
fact: Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars are small rocky planets.
fact: Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune are giant planets with no solid surface.
fact: Venus is the hottest planet, because its thick air traps heat.
fact: Saturn has the brightest rings, made of pieces of ice and rock.
fact: Mars looks red because its dust contains rust.
fact: Pluto is a dwarf planet, not one of the eight planets: it is small, and many other small icy worlds like it go around the Sun far out beyond Neptune.
fact: The farther a planet is from the Sun, the longer it takes to go around it.
fact: The Earth is the only planet known to have life.
exercise: What is the solar system? | The Sun and everything that goes around it | All the stars we can see at night | The Earth and its Moon | The Sun and the Moon only
exercise: How many planets are in the solar system? | Eight | Nine | Seven | Twelve
exercise: Which planet is closest to the Sun? | Mercury | Venus | Earth | Mars
exercise: Which planet is the biggest? | Jupiter | Saturn | Neptune | Earth
exercise: Which planet is farthest from the Sun? | Neptune | Pluto | Uranus | Saturn
exercise: Which planet is the hottest? | Venus, because its thick air traps heat | Mercury, because it is closest to the Sun | Mars, because it is red | Jupiter, because it is biggest
exercise: Which planets are small and rocky? | Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars | Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune | Earth, Jupiter, Saturn and Pluto | Mars, Jupiter, Uranus and Neptune
exercise: Why could you not land on Jupiter? | It has no solid surface | It is too small to land on | It is covered with deep oceans of water | It moves too fast to catch
exercise: Why is Mars red? | Its dust contains rust | It is very hot like fire | It is covered with red plants | It reflects light from Jupiter
exercise: What is Pluto? | A dwarf planet | The ninth planet | A moon of Neptune | A small star
exercise: Which planet has the brightest rings? | Saturn | Jupiter | Mars | Venus
exercise: Which planet takes the longest to go around the Sun? | Neptune | Mercury | Jupiter | Earth
exercise: What are Saturn's rings made of? | Pieces of ice and rock | One solid sheet of metal | Clouds of gas | Light from the Sun
exercise: Which planet comes right after the Earth, going outward from the Sun? | Mars | Venus | Jupiter | Mercury
exercise: Which planet is known to have life? | Only the Earth | Mars and the Earth | Venus and the Earth | All the rocky planets
test: A rocket leaves the Earth and flies outward. Which planet could it pass first? | Mars | Venus | Mercury | Saturn
test: Which is true? | A year on Mercury is shorter than a year on the Earth | A year on Neptune is shorter than a year on the Earth | All planets have years of the same length | Mercury takes the longest to go around the Sun
test: Which group are all giant planets? | Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune | Earth, Mars, Venus, Mercury | Jupiter, Mars, Saturn, Earth | Pluto, Neptune, Venus, Uranus
test: A girl says the closest planet to the Sun must be the hottest. Why is she wrong? | Venus is hotter because its thick air holds heat | Mercury is the farthest planet | The Sun does not warm the planets | Neptune is the hottest planet
test: If you made a model with the Sun as a football, how big would the Earth be? | Like a peppercorn | Like a tennis ball | Like a beach ball | Like a grain of dust far smaller than sand
test: Which planet is between Venus and Mars? | Earth | Mercury | Jupiter | Saturn
test: How many planets are farther from the Sun than the Earth? | Five | Three | Two | Seven
test: A space probe lands on a planet with a red, dusty, rocky ground. Where is it? | On Mars | On Jupiter | On Saturn | On Neptune
test: Why is Pluto no longer counted among the planets? | It is a small dwarf planet among many like it | It has fallen into the Sun | It was found to be a star | It moved out of the solar system
test: which planet's the biggest one again | Jupiter | Saturn | Earth | Neptune
test: how come mars looks kinda red | Its dust has rust in it | It is the hottest planet | It is covered in red lava | It is the closest planet to the Sun
test: Tom says Mercury's the hottest planet cos it's closest to the Sun. true? | No, Venus is hottest because its thick air traps heat | Yes, the closest planet must be the hottest | Yes, Mercury is hotter than all the others by far | No, Jupiter is hottest because it is biggest
test: my cousin says there's nine planets, Pluto too. right? | No, there are eight; Pluto is a dwarf planet | Yes, nine, and Pluto is the ninth | No, there are ten if you count the Moon | Yes, nine, but Pluto is the first one
exam: State the number of bodies presently classified as planets within the solar system. | Eight | Nine | Seven | Ten
exam: Identify, from among the following, the planet of greatest dimensions. | Jupiter | Saturn | Neptune | Earth
exam: Identify the principal reason for which Venus possesses the highest surface temperature of all the planets. | Its dense atmosphere retains heat | It is the planet nearest the Sun | It is composed chiefly of molten metal | It rotates with exceptional rapidity
exam: Select the response that is consistent with the established facts concerning the present classification of Pluto. | It is designated a dwarf planet | It is designated the ninth planet | It is designated a moon of Neptune | It is designated a star
